\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {6}{\ignorespaces \textbf  {Gym control under binary task-success reward, trained to plateau (3 seeds).} Solid: mean pass rate across curriculum bins; dashed: the \emph  {official} task (MountainCar flag / CartPole survive-400). Under the practical drop-constant-group estimator, the target-only arm (gray) remains empirically frozen; all-fail groups receive zero weights. A uniform-over-bins control (green) cracks both tasks but does not end at \(1.000\) in every seed; on MountainCar it is roughly \(3\times \) slower to hard-task 0.9. The gated FrontierMax stack converges to $1.000{\pm }0.000$.}}{15}{figure.66}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gym}{{6}{15}{\textbf {Gym control under binary task-success reward, trained to plateau (3 seeds).} Solid: mean pass rate across curriculum bins; dashed: the \emph {official} task (MountainCar flag / CartPole survive-400). Under the practical drop-constant-group estimator, the target-only arm (gray) remains empirically frozen; all-fail groups receive zero weights. A uniform-over-bins control (green) cracks both tasks but does not end at \(1.000\) in every seed; on MountainCar it is roughly \(3\times \) slower to hard-task 0.9. The gated FrontierMax stack converges to $1.000{\pm }0.000$}{figure.66}{}}
